# The build context for the SCORED image.
#
# Everything here is excluded from the image, so the image contains only the
# submission itself: the dispatcher, the five track sources, the shared
# core, and the vendored toolchain.
#
# vendor/ is deliberately NOT excluded — that is where the vendored Rust
# toolchain lives, and the build runs with --network=none, so it has to
# come from the context. Run tooling/vendor-toolchain.sh before the hack.

# Build cache and VCS
target/
.git/
.gitignore

# Host build output. build-all.sh rebuilds these inside the image, so
# shipping the developer's stale copies would put binaries of unknown
# provenance into the scored context and could hide a broken build.
bin/

# Test scratch left behind by local runs
verification/data2/
verification/tmp2/

# Verification infrastructure — never part of the submission
verification/
tooling/
docs/

# Generated fixtures — large, and reproducible with gen-fixtures.py
verification/data/
*.profdata
*.profraw

# Per-track documentation and metadata
tracks/*/verification/
tracks/*/PERF.md
tracks/*/README.md

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# CI and editor config that the container has no use for
.github/
*.log
